scenario.en:
import http from 'node:http';
import zlib from 'node:zlib';

http.createServer((req, res) => {
  if (req.url === '/export') {
    const body = zlib.gzipSync(tenMegabytes); // ~250ms of pure CPU
    return res.end(body);
  }
  res.end('ok'); // /health, /login, etc.
}).listen(3000);

While one /export is compressing, 50 other requests hit /health and /login. What happens to their latency, and why does the /export route's own dashboard look fine?

